# Parts talk through Memory

Shared state is the `Memory` dict bus (`donkeycar/memory.py`), not hidden globals.

- Parts read inputs and write outputs by key via `Vehicle.add`.
- Do not couple parts by importing each other for runtime data.
- Keep `run` small; heavy I/O belongs in threaded parts (`threaded=True`).
- Templates (`donkeycar/templates/`) are what users run — update them for first-class features.
- See workflow: `.cursor/workflows/add-part.md`
